00:10:16.553 --> 00:10:18.480
Did you know you were
gonna, did you wanna go

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:21.090
out on your own first or did
you like doing the pgv thing?

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.000
Like what, what, how did that all go down?

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.870
- I, I, Sonny was working

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:28.590
for Phil Specter and so I would go,

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:31.740
you know and I was staying
with Sonny even though he said

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:34.890
I don't find you particularly
attractive, which was good.

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:37.085
And so, so

00:10:37.085 --> 00:10:38.310
(Kelly laughing)

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:39.810
We were sharing a bedroom.

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:41.430
So I went to this.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:44.160
So I came, he came home one night, no

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.780
it was the daytime in the afternoon.

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:47.370
And I was making the bed

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.710
and I was singing and he peeped his head

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.960
around the doorway and
said, "Was that you?"

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:55.300
And I said, "Yeah" because
everybody in my family sings

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:58.200
they're from the south and
everybody sings, you know?

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.480
And, and so he said, "Well, you sing".

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:02.100
And I said, "Well, yeah".

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:06.060
And so then he took me to
the, he took me to the studio

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:10.072
and Darlene didn't show
up she, her car was

00:11:10.072 --> 00:11:14.490
got screwed up. And so
Philip asked me to go in.

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:16.860
And so I went in and then I stayed

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:20.411
until Lovin' Feelin' and
I was the only girl on it.

00:11:20.411 --> 00:11:22.170
(audience cheering &amp; clapping)

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:24.900
- So rad, I just did not know

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:26.250
- Wait, I'm gonna tell you one
- any of that.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:27.960
- Right, I have to tell
you one more thing.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:30.300
So in the old days

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:33.900
we sang in front of a
speaker, no headphones.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:37.380
So we were all around this
little speaker, like about yay

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:42.180
and yay and Philip would say,
"Cher, could you move back?"

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:43.110
And I'd say, "Yeah."

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:44.700
And then he'd say, "Cher,
can you move back?"

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:47.850
Well, I'm like back there and
Darlene's making fun of me

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.680
which Darlene did really well.

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:52.560
And he said, "It's great,
but you just cut through too

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:53.393
much."

00:11:53.393 --> 00:11:57.030
So that was my first experience
with singing background.

00:11:57.030 --> 00:11:59.370
And I really, I wasn't good to do it

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:02.430
for other people because
I was too nervous.

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:03.840
And also I didn't know what I was doing.

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:05.220
I had no idea what I, like,

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:08.160
he would say, "Darlene, Darlene,
sing me what you're doing.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.960
Juanita, tell me what,
sing me what you're doing."

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:11.970
I thought if he asked
me, I'm going to pass

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:15.060
out on the floor 'cause I
have no idea what I'm doing.

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:16.410
So, but he never did.

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:20.790
So, but I only knew what I was doing.

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:23.580
I just didn't have the nerve to say

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:26.230
this is what I'm doing,
because I really didn't know.

